Shape of the parity unit (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:telemetry/LiveSignalMonitor)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
requiredCount=4 = 4 strings. 0 charts, 0 maps, 0 named panels. Data sources: none declared (the page
renders from the shared live SSE stream / local state). The web page is a thin wrapper that mounts the
shared LiveSignalTail inside a PageContainer, driven by the shared useLiveSignalStream SSE hook
(web/src/features/telemetry/hooks/useLiveSignalStream.ts → useRealtimeEvents). The native port reproduces
the whole tree natively and reads the layered live state (ADR-004) rather than re-fetching history.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
- LiveSignalMonitorPage : UserControl — mounts the shared PageContainer (title liveMonitor.title, subtitle
  liveMonitor.subtitle, the live connection TsBadge in the header Actions) whose PageContent is the tail
  TsGlassPanel: the filter TsInput (search-prefixed), the Pause/Resume + Auto-scroll + Clear TsButtons, the
  four TsStatCards (Signals/sec, Buffer Size [+ "/ 500" sub-line], Unique Signals, Filtered) and the
  scrolling five-column table (Time / Signal / Value / Type / Freshness) — the Type cell is a semantic
  TsBadge, the Value cell tints from the same number→info / boolean→warning / string→success token map the
  web uses, and the Freshness cell is the TsFreshnessIndicator (ADR-013 two-minute window). Thin renderer:
  every label/value/visibility flows from LiveSignalMonitorDisplay; live SSE events arrive through the
  injected ILiveSignalMonitorFeed and are marshalled onto the UI thread before reaching the view-model; a
  1 Hz DispatcherQueueTimer drives the rate window; Group automation peer; tokens only (no literal colours).
- LiveSignalMonitorPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Owns the
  newest-first rolling buffer (cap 500, web TAIL_MAX), the signals/sec counter (web's 1 Hz reset), the
  pause / auto-scroll / filter controls and the connection state; ApplyVehicleUpdate / SetConnected /
  SetConnecting / SetErrored / SetFilter / TogglePaused / ToggleAutoScroll / Clear / SetVehicle /
  AdvanceRateWindow; projects LiveSignalMonitorDisplay. No I/O in the view.
- LiveSignalMonitorProjection / LiveSignalMonitorModel / LiveSignalMonitorDisplay — pure projection (no
  WinUI types) resolving every liveMonitor.* key on every call (the 4 manifest keys + the full tail label
  set), the filtered rows + unique/filtered/buffer/rate stat values (fmtInt port), and the
  loading/empty/streaming/error body-state flags. LiveSignalTailParser — the native port of the web
  handleVehicleUpdate firehose: the vehicle-scope filter, the cold[] / tables{} / signals{} (→ payload
  fallback) shapes, detectType and String(value) coercion, reserved-key + compound-value skipping.
  LiveSignalMonitorRegistration — RouteName="LiveSignalMonitor" (matches RouteTable.cs
  Page("LiveSignalMonitor","live-monitor",TelemetrySignals)), Slug, TailMax. PII-safe diagnostics (view.opened only).
- ILiveSignalMonitorFeed / EmptyLiveSignalMonitorFeed (no-backend default the shell-registered page mounts
  against — renders the Disconnected + waiting initial state) / LiveStoreSignalMonitorFeed (the live-store
  adapter binding L1 LiveSignalStore.VehicleUpdated + LiveConnectionMonitor → LiveConnectionMapping.IsLive,
  ADR-004; never reconstructs history from the stream).
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("LiveSignalMonitor", () => new FeatureViews.Telemetry.LiveSignalMonitorPage()).

i18n note (R3/ADR-014)
----------------------
Every liveMonitor.* key is resolved through keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <web default>) flowing through
ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization (resw lookup -> English fallback), exactly as the web resolves the
inline t(key, default) fallbacks. All keys already exist in apps/windows/Strings/*.resw; zero hardcoded
literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched. The web i18n key "liveMonitor.filterPlaceholder"
necessarily contains the substring the placeholder gate forbids, so its single call site carries an explicit
`// parity:allow` opt-out with reason (PLACEHOLDER_ALLOWED=1) — it is a real translation key, not a stub.

